// ZenTomato — template for local, private build settings.
//
// HOW TO USE THIS FILE
//
//     cp Config/Secrets.example.xcconfig Config/Secrets.xcconfig
//
// then fill in the values you need. `Config/Secrets.xcconfig` is git-ignored
// and is the only file on your machine that holds a real credential.
//
// THIS FILE IS COMMITTED AND EVERY VALUE IN IT IS EMPTY, ON PURPOSE. It exists
// so the repository documents which keys are needed without ever holding one.
// If you ever find a value here, that is a leak: remove it, and rotate the
// credential it exposed.
//
// You do NOT need any of these to build and run what exists today. Nothing in
// the app reads a Todoist credential yet.

// --- Todoist -----------------------------------------------------------------
// From the Todoist developer console. NOT NEEDED YET — no code reads either of
// these, and Config/App.xcconfig does not declare them. They are listed here so
// that when the Todoist feature is built you already know what it will ask for.
TODOIST_CLIENT_ID =
TODOIST_CLIENT_SECRET =

// --- Signing -----------------------------------------------------------------
// Your ten-character Apple Developer Team ID. Required ONLY to install on a
// physical iPhone; leave it empty to build and test on the simulator.
//
// Find it at https://developer.apple.com/account under Membership details, or
// run: security find-identity -v -p codesigning
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
